{"lines":[{"t":"Sample answers for Writing tasks","y":0.044929396700598367,"w":0.30566037495930987,"h":0.017650834403080906,"c":1,"x":0.098113209690156342},{"c":1,"x":0.096129451734186369,"y":0.092973519171687058,"w":0.34552322387695317,"t":"TEST 3, WRITING TASK 1","h":0.023778673007950335},{"w":0.19622641245524086,"h":0.01458152971769644,"t":"SAMPLE ANSWER","x":0.096226416385107427,"c":1,"y":0.13222079606490955},{"h":0.01855281932669206,"w":0.66800120035807298,"c":1,"t":"This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 6.0 score:","y":0.16965275706779803,"x":0.096185395673811722},{"y":0.19767441890308046,"h":0.020348836582952612,"x":0.096226419276206149,"w":0.79811319986979168,"t":"A hydroelectric power station can generate electric power by using the energy of water flowing from","c":1},{"x":0.094339632235813112,"h":0.020348836582952723,"c":1,"y":0.21947674449052523,"t":"high level to low level. It works different functions in day and night.","w":0.54528299967447924},{"c":1,"h":0.021841514401319539,"x":0.094289488431636342,"y":0.24840906261492424,"t":"In the day time, water in the high-level reservoir go through the intake under the dam which is","w":0.77179412841796879},{"h":0.01895505564815736,"c":1,"y":0.27180232560682793,"w":0.76415095011393241,"x":0.096226411618092977,"t":"only open in day time. Then the water flow into the power station in which there is a generator."},{"h":0.020539153372063024,"w":0.78679244995117181,"t":"The generator is operated by a reversible turbines that can transfer the water flowing force to the","x":0.094339624017609175,"y":0.29204107798900925,"c":1},{"t":"mechanical force which is the power of the generator. The generated electricity then goes to the","y":0.31386392804829311,"w":0.76981129964192718,"c":1,"x":0.096226425593194165,"h":0.021891885299584635},{"c":1,"t":"national grid through the power lines.","x":0.096226412306655976,"y":0.33568677785408596,"h":0.018964384884522123,"w":0.30754717508951823},{"y":0.36482558109337204,"w":0.8018868001302083,"t":"On the other hand in the night time, the power station works in a reversed way. It pumps water from","h":0.020348837807181663,"c":1,"x":0.096226411177081181},{"w":0.76801294962565114,"t":"the low-level reservoir to high-level reservoir to provide the enough water for day time's work.","c":1,"y":0.38502710429522724,"x":0.096173485095092229,"h":0.021675276358412154},{"w":0.79811319986979168,"h":0.019040884500290511,"c":1,"y":0.40843023258397093,"x":0.096226418821560369,"t":"The water is pumped by the same reversible turbines trom low-level reservoir. So the power station"},{"y":0.42861340913629131,"t":"actually consumes energy at night. But that is in order to generate more power in the day time.","h":0.021585442441418801,"c":1,"x":0.096171624950742204,"w":0.76612869262695316},{"c":1,"w":0.78301884969075508,"h":0.020348836582952723,"t":"In a conclusion, a hydroelectric power station can generate power is based on the differce heighth","x":0.096226431357452402,"y":0.45784883726811665},{"w":0.79066843668619802,"h":0.021312298609448277,"x":0.096171668051175913,"c":1,"y":0.47941847658702197,"t":"of water level. In day time, it uses the natural water energy. Meanwhile in the night, it transters the"},{"x":0.096226422208772908,"y":0.50145348867315542,"w":0.43396224975585934,"h":0.020369361392646779,"c":1,"t":"water to create and store the energy for the next day."},{"t":"Here is the examiner's comment:","w":0.3018868001302083,"h":0.014762516046213037,"y":0.53915275979917499,"c":1,"x":0.0962264111113664},{"x":0.14146947320451686,"h":0.018579983741848438,"t":"The answer covers the key features of the process and provides an overview of this","y":0.575492976436485,"w":0.75669204711914073,"c":1},{"t":"process in the final paragraph. The detail is not always clear, but the key features","w":0.73595718383789066,"y":0.59347723288223897,"x":0.14145640724292993,"c":1,"h":0.020425178273192346},{"y":0.61482558146425381,"w":0.74528299967447909,"h":0.016111517136149001,"c":1,"t":"are adequately highlighted. Intormation is arranged coherently and there is a clear","x":0.14150944346705938},{"w":0.71509435017903633,"c":1,"y":0.63222079603119308,"t":"overall progression. Cohesive devices are used to signal different stages of the","h":0.017488506547293725,"x":0.14150942861889321},{"w":0.72830190022786456,"h":0.019053945186355392,"c":1,"t":"process [Then | On the other hand | So | In a conclusion | Meanwhile], and there","x":0.14150942715765874,"y":0.64955070594498443},{"h":0.017650834403080795,"w":0.73018870035807293,"t":"is some use of pronouns for reference [It | which | that]. The range of vocabulary","x":0.13962263071250428,"y":0.66848523777711788,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.13958332108938179,"t":"is adequate for the task [energy | operated by | transfer | mechanical], in spite of","h":0.018834697419779944,"y":0.68727940845578872,"w":0.73216898600260416},{"y":0.70635430051078896,"c":1,"w":0.74150945027669279,"t":"some errors in word form [a reversed way] and spelling [differce heighth]. There is","x":0.14150942572652941,"h":0.016046213093709905},{"c":1,"x":0.14150943339590508,"w":0.73773585001627606,"t":"a mix of simple and complex sentence forms and grammatical control is generally","h":0.016046213093709905,"y":0.72528883201846051},{"c":1,"x":0.14150944201220519,"t":"adequate, though there are some errors in the use of articles.","w":0.55849054972330736,"y":0.74418604625187734,"h":0.017441860977584156},{"w":0.03584905624389649,"y":0.95348837181342727,"t":"132","c":1,"h":0.01453488414798676,"x":0.096226415231396537}],"w":2400,"h":3115}